    "knowledge_point": "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Tangent Function",
    "problem": "If $tan⁡x=3,$ for some $x$, find the value of $tan⁡(x+5\\pi )+2.$",
    "worked_solution": "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡x=tan⁡(x+5\\cdot \\pi )=tan⁡(x+5\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $tan⁡x=3,$ we get that $tan⁡(x+5\\pi )=3.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\ntan⁡(x+5\\pi )+2=(3)+2=5.\n$$",
